IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er2-common`
IMPORT `er2-allocation`
IMPORT `er2-claims`
IMPORT `er2-record-of-employment`
IMPORT `er2-seat`

-- Worked cases for er2-seat (regulations 19 to 34): at least one case per question, in the facts a real person in the seat would state.
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the regulation named beside it and was decided before the run. One #ASSERT per line.
-- Calendar facts used: 4 March 2026 is a Wednesday (its week is Sunday 1 March to Saturday 7 March); 25 December 2026 is a Friday.
-- Argument order is the order of the question's inputs in er2-seat.l4.

§ `Your record of employment (regs 19 to 21)`

-- Kofi is laid off by Maple Foods, his employer, in insurable employment: his earnings are interrupted. Args: employer or former employer, bankrupt,
-- trustee, employed in insurable employment, earnings interrupted.
#ASSERT     `Must the person or company I worked for complete a record of employment for me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- the trustee of a bankrupt employer is an "employer" for subsections (2) to (4) (reg 19(1))
#ASSERT     `Must the person or company I worked for complete a record of employment for me` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- someone who was never his employer owes him nothing under regulation 19(2)
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the person or company I worked for complete a record of employment for me` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- no interruption of earnings yet
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the person or company I worked for complete a record of employment for me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)

-- Kofi's interruption began on Monday 2 March; Maple Foods learned of it on Wednesday 4 March: five days after the later, 9 March.
#ASSERT `By what date must my employer give me my paper record of employment` (YMD 2026 3 2) (YMD 2026 3 4) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9
#ASSERT     `Was my paper record of employment given to me in time` (YMD 2026 3 2) (YMD 2026 3 4) (YMD 2026 3 9)
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my paper record of employment given to me in time` (YMD 2026 3 2) (YMD 2026 3 4) (YMD 2026 3 10))
#ASSERT     `Was the Commission's copy of my paper record of employment sent in time` (YMD 2026 3 2) (YMD 2026 3 4) (YMD 2026 3 9)
#ASSERT NOT (`Was the Commission's copy of my paper record of employment sent in time` (YMD 2026 3 2) (YMD 2026 3 4) (YMD 2026 3 10))

-- Naledi's employer pays monthly (12 pay periods); her pay period ended 31 March and her interruption began 10 March: the earlier of 5 April and 25 March.
#ASSERT `By what date must my employer send my electronic record of employment to the Commission` (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 3 10) 12 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 25
-- an employer on a weekly pay cycle (52 periods) has only limb (i): 5 April
#ASSERT `By what date must my employer send my electronic record of employment to the Commission` (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 3 10) 52 EQUALS YMD 2026 4 5
#ASSERT     `Was my electronic record of employment sent to the Commission in time` (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 3 10) 12 (YMD 2026 3 25)
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my electronic record of employment sent to the Commission in time` (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 3 10) 12 (YMD 2026 3 26))
#ASSERT     `Has my employer kept and retained its copy of my record of employment` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my employer kept and retained its copy of my record of employment` FALSE)

-- Ines's employer could not deliver her copy for reasons beyond its control. Args: unable, knows her mailing address.
#ASSERT `What must my employer do with my record of employment if it could not deliver it to me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `er2 mail the copy to the insured person`
#ASSERT `What must my employer do with my record of employment if it could not deliver it to me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `er2 retain the copy until the earliest of the Commission's request, the person's request and 52 weeks after completion`
#ASSERT `What must my employer do with my record of employment if it could not deliver it to me` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `er2 regulation 19(4) does not apply because delivery was not prevented for reasons beyond the employer's control`
-- completed 5 January 2026; nobody asks: 52 weeks (364 days) later, 4 January 2027
#ASSERT `Until what day may my employer keep my record of employment without sending it` (YMD 2026 1 5) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 4
-- the Commission asks on 1 June 2026; Ines asks on 3 March 2026: the first of the three events is hers
#ASSERT `Until what day may my employer keep my record of employment without sending it` (YMD 2026 1 5) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 3) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 3
#ASSERT `Until what day may my employer keep my record of employment without sending it` (YMD 2026 1 5) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1

-- Omar's employer has gone out of business and cannot be found: he has applied for benefits and may give a statement. Args: failed to give me, failed to give
-- the Commission, not available, unable (records destroyed or lost), I have applied.
#ASSERT     `May I give the Commission a statement of my hours and earnings instead of a record of employment` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT     `May I give the Commission a statement of my hours and earnings instead of a record of employment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I give the Commission a statement of my hours and earnings instead of a record of employment` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May I give the Commission a statement of my hours and earnings instead of a record of employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Priya's employer is bankrupt and no record was provided to her. Args: bankrupt, trustee, not given to me, not given to the Commission.
#ASSERT     `Must the Commission work out my hours and earnings from my bankrupt employer's records` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Commission work out my hours and earnings from my bankrupt employer's records` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Commission work out my hours and earnings from my bankrupt employer's records` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `Are the hours on my record of employment the hours determined under Part I of the Act` 840 840
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the hours on my record of employment the hours determined under Part I of the Act` 840 839)
#ASSERT     `Are the insurable earnings on my record of employment those determined and allocated` 4200.5 4200.5
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the insurable earnings on my record of employment those determined and allocated` 4200.5 4200)

§ `How your hours and earnings are allocated (regs 22 to 24.3)`

-- Tomas's job ran from 5 January to 4 April 2026 (90 days); his qualifying period is 1 March 2026 to 27 February 2027: it begins inside his job.
#ASSERT     `Does the Commission allocate the hours of my job across my qualifying period` (YMD 2026 1 5) (YMD 2026 4 4) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2027 2 27)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the Commission allocate the hours of my job across my qualifying period` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 8 31) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2027 2 27))
-- 360 hours over 90 days is 4 a day; the 35 days shared with the qualifying period carry 140 hours. Args: job first, last; record first, last; QP first, last; hours; evidence?; hours by evidence
#ASSERT `How many hours of my job count within my qualifying period` (YMD 2026 1 5) (YMD 2026 4 4) (YMD 2026 1 5) (YMD 2026 4 4) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2027 2 27) 360 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 140
-- 100 hours: 38.9 hours, counted as 39 (reg 22(2))
#ASSERT `How many hours of my job count within my qualifying period` (YMD 2026 1 5) (YMD 2026 4 4) (YMD 2026 1 5) (YMD 2026 4 4) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2027 2 27) 100 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 39
-- his employer can show he really worked 77 hours in the qualifying period: that governs
#ASSERT `How many hours of my job count within my qualifying period` (YMD 2026 1 5) (YMD 2026 4 4) (YMD 2026 1 5) (YMD 2026 4 4) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2027 2 27) 360 TRUE 77 EQUALS JUST 77
-- a job of 731 days (2024-2025), its record covering 2025 only (365 days, 5 hours a day), qualifying period from 1 July 2025: 184 days, 920 hours
#ASSERT `How many hours of my job count within my qualifying period` (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2025 12 31) (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 12 31) (YMD 2025 7 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) 1825 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 920
-- a job wholly inside the qualifying period: regulation 22 does not decide
#ASSERT `How many hours of my job count within my qualifying period` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 8 31) (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 8 31) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2027 2 27) 500 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Mei is paid overtime for a pay period. Args: kind, basis, on unpaid leave or quit, fixed-term, irregular, solely commissions, salary and irregular commissions.
#ASSERT `Which rule of regulation 23 allocates this payment of mine to a pay period` `er2 overtime pay` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er2 proportionately over the pay period in which it is paid`
-- a bonus paid after she quit: moved to the last pay period for which regular pay is paid (23(1.1))
#ASSERT `Which rule of regulation 23 allocates this payment of mine to a pay period` `er2 bonuses` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er2 proportionately over the last pay period for which regular salary, wages or commissions are paid`
-- ordinary pay for work done in the pay period: in proportion to the hours worked each day (23(1)(a)(i))
#ASSERT `Which rule of regulation 23 allocates this payment of mine to a pay period` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er2 to the pay period in proportion to the hours worked during each day of the period`
-- a fixed-term contract paid irregularly: over the term of the contract (23(2))
#ASSERT `Which rule of regulation 23 allocates this payment of mine to a pay period` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 not paid in respect of a pay period` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er2 proportionately over the term of the contract`
-- a salesperson paid only commission: 23(3)
#ASSERT `Which rule of regulation 23 allocates this payment of mine to a pay period` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 not paid in respect of a pay period` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `er2 proportionately over the shorter of the period of employment and the last 52 weeks, excluding weeks of unpaid leave for a reason in subsection 12(3) of the Act`
-- none of (1) to (3): subsection (4)
#ASSERT `Which rule of regulation 23 allocates this payment of mine to a pay period` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period but neither for work performed during it nor for a period of leave` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er2 proportionately over the shorter of the period of employment and the last 52 weeks`
-- Wanda's pay of 600 for the pay period is unpaid for a reason in subsection 2(2) of the Insurable Earnings and Collection of Premiums Regulations
#ASSERT     `Is my unpaid remuneration allocated as if I had been paid it in the normal course of business` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my unpaid remuneration allocated as if I had been paid it in the normal course of business` FALSE)
-- 3 days of a 10-day period carry 3/10 of 1000; an empty period is not covered
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is allocated to a stretch of days when it is allocated proportionately` 1000 3 10 EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is allocated to a stretch of days when it is allocated proportionately` 1000 3 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Xavier is paid 700 for a pay period of 40 hours, 8 of them on the day
#ASSERT `How much of this pay is allocated to one day in proportion to the hours I worked` 700 8 40 EQUALS JUST 140
#ASSERT `How much of this pay is allocated to one day in proportion to the hours I worked` 700 8 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Yara's 14 days of leave were paid at 95.50 a day
#ASSERT `How much of my pay for a period of leave is allocated to it at the rate at which the leave was paid` 95.5 14 EQUALS 1337
-- Zed sells on commission: 400 days of employment, the last 52 weeks (364 days) are used; with 2 weeks of unpaid leave for a 12(3) reason, 350
#ASSERT `Over how many days are my commission earnings allocated, leaving out my weeks of unpaid leave` 400 0 EQUALS JUST 364
#ASSERT `Over how many days are my commission earnings allocated, leaving out my weeks of unpaid leave` 400 2 EQUALS JUST 350
#ASSERT `Over how many days are my commission earnings allocated, leaving out my weeks of unpaid leave` 14 3 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Over how many days are my other earnings allocated when none of subsections (1) to (3) applies` 400 EQUALS 364
#ASSERT `Over how many days are my other earnings allocated when none of subsections (1) to (3) applies` 100 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT     `May my employer estimate my insurable earnings for my last pay period` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May my employer estimate my insurable earnings for my last pay period` TRUE FALSE)

-- Lena's job ran Wednesday 4 to Tuesday 17 March 2026 (14 days) and earned 2800. Her week of Sunday 1 March has 4 of those days: 800.
-- Args: job first, last; a day in the week; QP first, last; earnings on the record; lay-off or separation part; evidence?; evidence amount
#ASSERT `How much of my insurable earnings are allocated to this week of my qualifying period` (YMD 2026 3 4) (YMD 2026 3 17) (YMD 2026 3 4) (YMD 2025 9 1) (YMD 2026 8 30) 2800 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 800
-- 700 of the 2800 was separation pay: (2800 - 700) x 4 / 14 = 600
#ASSERT `How much of my insurable earnings are allocated to this week of my qualifying period` (YMD 2026 3 4) (YMD 2026 3 17) (YMD 2026 3 4) (YMD 2025 9 1) (YMD 2026 8 30) 2800 700 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 600
#ASSERT `How much of my insurable earnings are allocated to this week of my qualifying period` (YMD 2026 3 4) (YMD 2026 3 17) (YMD 2026 3 4) (YMD 2025 9 1) (YMD 2026 8 30) 2800 700 TRUE 450 EQUALS JUST 450
#ASSERT `How much of my insurable earnings are allocated to this week of my qualifying period` (YMD 2026 3 4) (YMD 2026 3 17) (YMD 2026 3 22) (YMD 2025 9 1) (YMD 2026 8 30) 2800 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Raj is paid 5000 on lay-off from a job where he earned 20000 in the calculation period: the lesser of 5000 and 18% of 20000 (3600)
#ASSERT `How much of my pay on lay-off or separation counts as insurable earnings in my qualifying period` 5000 20000 EQUALS 3600
#ASSERT `How much of my pay on lay-off or separation counts as insurable earnings in my qualifying period` 3000 20000 EQUALS 3000
-- Sofia is self-employed under Part VII.1; earnings from a job she left without just cause are left out of her rate. Args: misconduct, left without just
-- cause, day earned, QP first, QP last, earlier benefit period?, its first day
#ASSERT     `Are these insurable earnings left out of my rate of weekly benefits as a self-employed person` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2025 10 5) (YMD 2026 10 3) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT     `Are these insurable earnings left out of my rate of weekly benefits as a self-employed person` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2025 10 5) (YMD 2026 10 3) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1)
-- earned 15 January 2026, before her earlier benefit period began on 1 March 2026
#ASSERT     `Are these insurable earnings left out of my rate of weekly benefits as a self-employed person` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2025 10 5) (YMD 2026 10 3) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Are these insurable earnings left out of my rate of weekly benefits as a self-employed person` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 4 1) (YMD 2025 10 5) (YMD 2026 10 3) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1))

§ `Weeks of benefits, the election and your claims (regs 25 to 26.1)`

-- Dara was paid 400 for one week (rate 400) and 200 for the next (rate 400): 100 + 50 = 150, so one week of benefits.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits am I considered to have been paid` (LIST 400, 200) (LIST 400, 400) EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits am I considered to have been paid` (LIST 400, 400, 100) (LIST 400, 400, 400) EQUALS JUST 2
-- two lists of different lengths: not covered
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits am I considered to have been paid` (LIST 400, 200) (LIST 400) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT     `Have I made my election between Part I and Part VII.1 benefits as the Regulations require` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I made my election between Part I and Part VII.1 benefits as the Regulations require` TRUE FALSE)
-- Wednesday 4 March 2026: three weeks after the week that ends Saturday 7 March is 28 March; after four weeks without a claim, one week: 14 March
#ASSERT `By what date must I make my claim for a week of unemployment` (YMD 2026 3 4) 0 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 28
#ASSERT `By what date must I make my claim for a week of unemployment` (YMD 2026 3 4) 4 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 14
#ASSERT     `Is my claim for this week of unemployment in time` (YMD 2026 3 4) 0 (YMD 2026 3 28)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my claim for this week of unemployment in time` (YMD 2026 3 4) 4 (YMD 2026 3 20))

-- Hana is pregnant: her period under section 22(2) runs from 1 February to 4 July 2026 and she has not served her one-week waiting period (7 days).
-- Args: reason, apprenticeship, work-sharing, first day of period, last day of period, days of waiting period not served.
#ASSERT `What is my period of eligibility for the purposes of excusing me from periodic claims` `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2026 7 4) 7 EQUALS JUST (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 2 1), (YMD 2026 7 11))
-- a sick claimant has no "period of eligibility" under this definition
#ASSERT `What is my period of eligibility for the purposes of excusing me from periodic claims` `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2026 7 4) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Hana on her initial claim: all four conditions met. Args: initial, first claim after 4 weeks, reason, apprenticeship, work-sharing, period first, last, waiting days,
-- claims every week, completed the form, form (i), (ii), (iii), Commission learned?, day it learned, the day asked about
#ASSERT     `Am I excused from making periodic claims on this day` TRUE FALSE `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2026 7 4) 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- Rob, on sickness benefits, is not excused: sickness is not in paragraph (2)(c)(i)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excused from making periodic claims on this day` TRUE FALSE `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2026 7 4) 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- Hana without the Commission's form
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excused from making periodic claims on this day` TRUE FALSE `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2026 7 4) 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- the Commission learned on 10 February that she fails a condition: from that date she must make periodic claims; before it, not
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excused from making periodic claims on this day` TRUE FALSE `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2026 7 4) 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 2 10) (YMD 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT     `Am I excused from making periodic claims on this day` TRUE FALSE `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2026 7 4) 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 5 10) (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- Hana must tell the Commission as soon as possible if she stops meeting a condition in a way that reduces her benefits, or has deductible earnings
#ASSERT     `Must I notify the Commission as soon as possible while I am excused from periodic claims` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT     `Must I notify the Commission as soon as possible while I am excused from periodic claims` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I notify the Commission as soon as possible while I am excused from periodic claims` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `By what day must I tell the Commission at the end of my period of eligibility` (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2026 7 4) EQUALS YMD 2026 7 4
#ASSERT     `Is this a condition of entitlement to benefits for the purposes of regulation 26.1` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this a condition of entitlement to benefits for the purposes of regulation 26.1` FALSE)

§ `If a claim is made for an incapacitated or a deceased person (reg 27)`

-- Grace claims for her father, who has dementia and meets the requirements of Part I.
#ASSERT     `Will the Commission authorize payment of the benefits to the person acting for an incapacitated claimant` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Will the Commission authorize payment of the benefits to the person acting for an incapacitated claimant` TRUE FALSE)
-- Hugo is the executor of a deceased claimant and makes the claim; she met the requirements when she died.
#ASSERT     `As the executor or administrator of a deceased claimant, will the Commission authorize payment of their benefits to me` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT     `As the executor or administrator of a deceased claimant, will the Commission authorize payment of their benefits to me` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`As the executor or administrator of a deceased claimant, will the Commission authorize payment of their benefits to me` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`As the executor or administrator of a deceased claimant, will the Commission authorize payment of their benefits to me` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Iris is the only heir of a man who left no will and a very small estate: everything in order. Args: entitled, intestate, too small for letters of administration,
-- too small for probate, Commission's form, declaration, undertaking, will exists, copy of will, others entitled, their release.
#ASSERT     `As a person entitled to succeed to a deceased claimant's property, will their benefits be payable to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- a will exists and there are other heirs: Jin needs the will and the others' releases
#ASSERT     `As a person entitled to succeed to a deceased claimant's property, will their benefits be payable to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`As a person entitled to succeed to a deceased claimant's property, will their benefits be payable to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- the estate is large enough to warrant letters of administration
#ASSERT NOT (`As a person entitled to succeed to a deceased claimant's property, will their benefits be payable to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

