§ `Whether you worked a full working week (regs 29 to 32)`

-- Boris is a railway employee paid by the mile; with a maximum weekly insurable earnings of 750 he needs at least 1500 in the two weeks.
#ASSERT     `As a railway employee paid by mileage, am I considered to have worked a full working week in each week of the two-week period` TRUE TRUE 1500 750
#ASSERT NOT (`As a railway employee paid by mileage, am I considered to have worked a full working week in each week of the two-week period` TRUE TRUE 1400 750)
-- Cleo works on a farm: five days and 35 hours make a full working week
#ASSERT     `In farming or horticulture, am I considered to have worked a full working week this week` TRUE 5 35
#ASSERT NOT (`In farming or horticulture, am I considered to have worked a full working week this week` TRUE 5 30)
-- Dev did not work on Christmas Day and worked his normal hours on each of the other four working days
#ASSERT     `Am I regarded as having worked a full working week although a holiday fell in the week` TRUE FALSE 4 4
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I regarded as having worked a full working week although a holiday fell in the week` TRUE FALSE 4 3)
-- Esi is paid monthly-like for a two-week period whatever work she does: 4 March is in a week wholly inside it
#ASSERT     `Is this week a full working week because my usual pay is for a period longer than a week` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 14) (YMD 2026 3 4)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this week a full working week because my usual pay is for a period longer than a week` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 14) (YMD 2026 3 15))
-- Femi runs a small business on his own account. Args: engaged in a business, employed, employer a corporation, voting share, own account, partnership,
-- co-adventure, controls hours elsewhere, minor extent, farming, a day in the week, proves did not work, proves minor extent.
#ASSERT     `Am I a self-employed person for the purposes of regulation 30` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0
#ASSERT     `Am I a self-employed person for the purposes of regulation 30` FALSE TRUE TRUE 0.41
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a self-employed person for the purposes of regulation 30` FALSE TRUE TRUE 0.4)
#ASSERT `Am I considered to have worked a full working week this week as a self-employed person or a person who controls their own hours` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 15) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the business is such a minor extent that a person would not normally rely on it: not regarded as a full working week (30(2))
#ASSERT `Am I considered to have worked a full working week this week as a self-employed person or a person who controls their own hours` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 15) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a farmer in the week of 1 December 2026 who proves he did not work: not considered to have worked a full working week (30(4))
#ASSERT `Am I considered to have worked a full working week this week as a self-employed person or a person who controls their own hours` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 12 1) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- nothing in subsection (1) describes the work: regulation 30 does not decide
#ASSERT `Am I considered to have worked a full working week this week as a self-employed person or a person who controls their own hours` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 15) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Gita cut her business time from 40 hours to 23.9: a reduction of more than 40%
#ASSERT     `Is this a week of unemployment for me as a self-employed person` 40 23.9
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this a week of unemployment for me as a self-employed person` 40 24)
-- the six circumstances considered in judging a minor extent
#ASSERT count `What circumstances are considered in judging whether my work is of such a minor extent` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT elem `er2 the time spent` `What circumstances are considered in judging whether my work is of such a minor extent`
#ASSERT     `Am I deemed to be not working as a self-employed person` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I deemed to be not working as a self-employed person` TRUE FALSE)
-- Hiro is a part-timer in a 20-hour week; full-time work nearby is 37.5 hours. Args: 29 or 30 applies, unit rate, normal number, part-time number?, full-time number, days normally worked.
#ASSERT `How many hours, days or shifts make a full working week for me` FALSE FALSE 20 TRUE 37.5 5 EQUALS JUST 37.5
#ASSERT `How many hours, days or shifts make a full working week for me` FALSE FALSE 40 FALSE 37.5 5 EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `How many hours, days or shifts make a full working week for me` FALSE TRUE 40 FALSE 37.5 5 EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `How many hours, days or shifts make a full working week for me` TRUE FALSE 40 FALSE 37.5 5 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Have I worked a full working week` 37.5 FALSE FALSE 20 TRUE 37.5 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I worked a full working week` 30 FALSE FALSE 20 TRUE 37.5 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I worked a full working week` 30 TRUE FALSE 20 TRUE 37.5 5 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT     `Is this a working day` (YMD 2026 3 4)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this a working day` (YMD 2026 3 7))
-- Christmas Day, a Friday and a holiday, is still a working day: only Saturday and Sunday are left out
#ASSERT     `Is this a working day` (YMD 2026 12 25)

§ `If you are a teacher (reg 33)`

-- Args: occupation is teaching, pre-elementary, elementary, secondary, technical or vocational.
#ASSERT     `Does my work count as teaching` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my work count as teaching` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `Is this period a non-teaching period` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this period a non-teaching period` TRUE FALSE)
-- Jamal taught in his qualifying period and claims for a summer week with regular benefits, no exception: barred. Args: taught, week in a non-teaching period, reason,
-- contract terminated, casual or substitute, qualifies on other work.
#ASSERT     `As a teacher, am I barred from benefits for a week of unemployment in a non-teaching period` TRUE TRUE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Kara's teaching contract has terminated
#ASSERT NOT (`As a teacher, am I barred from benefits for a week of unemployment in a non-teaching period` TRUE TRUE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Lia is on maternity benefits (section 22): not barred
#ASSERT NOT (`As a teacher, am I barred from benefits for a week of unemployment in a non-teaching period` TRUE TRUE `pregnancy` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Mo is on sickness benefits: barred (section 21 is not among the excepted sections)
#ASSERT     `As a teacher, am I barred from benefits for a week of unemployment in a non-teaching period` TRUE TRUE `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Nia qualifies on work other than teaching, which pays 300 a week against the 450 otherwise payable: limited to 300
#ASSERT `As a teacher who also qualifies on other work, what is the most I can be paid for a week in a non-teaching period` TRUE TRUE TRUE 300 450 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `As a teacher who also qualifies on other work, what is the most I can be paid for a week in a non-teaching period` TRUE TRUE FALSE 300 450 EQUALS 450

§ `If you have children: the family supplement (reg 34)`

#ASSERT     `Is the person I live with my cohabitating spouse or common-law partner for the purposes of regulation 34` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the person I live with my cohabitating spouse or common-law partner for the purposes of regulation 34` FALSE)
#ASSERT     `Is my Canada child benefit treated as an overpayment under the Income Tax Act for the purposes of the family supplement` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my Canada child benefit treated as an overpayment under the Income Tax Act for the purposes of the family supplement` FALSE)
-- Olu claims for the week containing Wednesday 4 March 2026 (Sunday 1 March): the Canada child benefit for February 2026 counts
#ASSERT `Which month's Canada child benefit counts for the week I am claiming for` (YMD 2026 3 4) EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 2 1), (YMD 2026 2 28)
-- Pia and her partner receive the Canada child benefit for 4 children, 2 of them under 7, on a family income of 23000: 48.60 + 17.40 + 2 x 2.60 = 71.20
#ASSERT `How much family supplement does the table give for my family income and my children` 23000 4 2 EQUALS JUST 71.2
-- an income of 26000 is above the last band of the table: not covered
#ASSERT `How much family supplement does the table give for my family income and my children` 26000 1 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the most my family supplement can be as a percentage of my weekly insurable earnings` 2026 EQUALS JUST (25%)
#ASSERT `What is the most my family supplement can be as a percentage of my weekly insurable earnings` 1998 EQUALS JUST (15%)
#ASSERT `What is the most my family supplement can be as a percentage of my weekly insurable earnings` 1996 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Pia's weekly insurable earnings are 400: the ceiling is 25% of 400 = 100, so the whole 71.20. Args: established, spouse also increased, family income, children, under 7,
-- weekly insurable earnings, day benefit period established, the week, (5) reduces it, children 12 to 15, children 16 or 17.
#ASSERT `By how much is my rate of weekly benefits increased for this week by the family supplement` TRUE FALSE 23000 4 2 400 (YMD 2026 1 5) (YMD 2026 3 4) FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST 71.2
-- with weekly insurable earnings of 200 the ceiling is 50
#ASSERT `By how much is my rate of weekly benefits increased for this week by the family supplement` TRUE FALSE 23000 4 2 200 (YMD 2026 1 5) (YMD 2026 3 4) FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST 50
-- her partner's benefits are increased as well: no increase for her
#ASSERT `By how much is my rate of weekly benefits increased for this week by the family supplement` TRUE TRUE 23000 4 2 400 (YMD 2026 1 5) (YMD 2026 3 4) FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- Quentin, a 1998 benefit period, week of 5 September 1999, reduced by (5): 31.25 + 2.20 for a child of 13
#ASSERT `By how much is my rate of weekly benefits increased for this week by the family supplement` TRUE FALSE 21000 1 0 300 (YMD 1998 6 1) (YMD 1999 9 5) TRUE 1 0 EQUALS JUST 33.45
-- a family income of 30000 is above the table: not covered
#ASSERT `By how much is my rate of weekly benefits increased for this week by the family supplement` TRUE FALSE 30000 1 0 400 (YMD 2026 1 5) (YMD 2026 3 4) FALSE 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
